From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:49:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D216 util: a spawn failure that Bun throws fails the spawn
 instead of hanging

Upstream: Bun's child_process.spawn throws some failures synchronously instead of emitting "error" (E2BIG for an
argument over the system limit, such as a shell command longer than 128 KiB on Linux). The cross-spawn spawner
launches inside an Effect.callback, so the throw becomes a defect; Shell.create only settles its startup on a typed
failure, so POST /api/shell never answers, and a shell tool call with such a command hangs its session.
Fixed: a synchronous spawn throw fails the spawn with the same PlatformError as an emitted error (Redacted arguments
stay redacted).
Scenarios: shell-api.test.ts "shell routes for unknown commands" (new requests; the oversized command answered
500 before D217, and never before this patch)
Upstream tests: packages/core/test/effect/cross-spawn-spawner.test.ts adds a test

diff --git a/packages/core/test/effect/cross-spawn-spawner.test.ts b/packages/core/test/effect/cross-spawn-spawner.test.ts
index 08abaff602..021e18a4b1 100644
--- a/packages/core/test/effect/cross-spawn-spawner.test.ts
+++ b/packages/core/test/effect/cross-spawn-spawner.test.ts
@@ -408,6 +408,23 @@ describe("cross-spawn spawner", () => {
       }),
     )
 
+    fx.effect(
+      "fails for an argument the system cannot pass",
+      Effect.gen(function* () {
+        if (process.platform === "win32") return
+        // Linux limits one argument to 128 KiB and every system limits the whole list.
+        const exit = yield* Effect.exit(
+          Effect.scoped(
+            Effect.flatMap(ChildProcess.make("echo", ["x".repeat(4 * 1024 * 1024)]), (handle) => handle.exitCode),
+          ),
+        )
+        expect(Exit.isFailure(exit)).toBe(true)
+        if (Exit.isSuccess(exit)) return
+        expect(Cause.hasDies(exit.cause)).toBe(false)
+        expect(PlatformError.isPlatformError(Cause.squash(exit.cause))).toBe(true)
+      }),
+    )
+
     fx.effect(
       "rejects NUL characters without exposing Redacted values",
       Effect.gen(function* () {
